# site.env.example: copy to site.env beside it (ignored by git), fill in, chmod 600. hpctests.py reads it (or the file
# HPCT_SITE names); nothing in it is ever printed, committed or put on a step's command line. Never paste its values
# into an issue, a PR or a session log.
#
# The ssh destination of the login node: a Host alias of your ssh config, given here or in a 0600 file of its own.
HPCT_HOST='<ssh alias>'
# HPCT_HOST_FILE='/path/to/a/0600/file/holding/the/alias'
#
# What sbatch needs (sent to the login node's login.env by `install`, through ssh's stdin).
HPCT_ACCOUNT='<account>'
HPCT_PARTITION='<standard partition>'
# The allocation's shape and name (defaults shown). Billing is per allocated hour, busy or idle.
# HPCT_JOB_NAME='expcore-tests'
# HPCT_CPUS='16'
# HPCT_MEM='30G'
# HPCT_HOURS='12'
# HPCT_MAX_ALIVE='2'        # at most this many allocations of ours alive at once (a running one and its successor)
#
# The nodes. The uv binary must be on a filesystem the nodes see; pin its version to the one that made uv.lock (CI's).
HPCT_UV='<absolute path of uv on the nodes>'
HPCT_UV_VERSION='0.11.19'
# HPCT_PYTHON='3.13'                          # a uv-managed Python, installed into the node's tmpfs root
# HPCT_NODE_ROOT='/tmp/expcore-hpct'          # the node's tmpfs; the boot appends -<uid> and refuses anything else
# HPCT_STEP_PATH='/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin'
# HPCT_LOGIN_DIR='.expcore-hpct'             # relative to the login node's home: alloc.sh, login.env, the ledger
#
# This host: where results are written (one directory per run) and where a run's payload is built (removed after).
HPCT_OUT='<a directory for results, outside every git worktree>'
# HPCT_WORK='<a scratch directory; the default is $TMPDIR>'
